    description: "cmd_dead_code_maybe (cli.py ~:9192-9207) builds Symbol(id, name, kind, language, path, span, meta) by hand for entrypoint detection instead of Symbol.from_dict, dropping supply_chain_tier (defaults to 1) and modifiers. detect_entrypoints reads both (tier>=3 rank penalties ~entrypoints.py:1735/1852; declaration-vs-definition dedup ~:1585), so vendored entrypoints are not demoted and declaration duplicates are not collapsed. Impact limited to --min-confidence > 0 (default 0.0). Fix: route through Symbol.from_dict like every other read path. Confirmed by reading, 2026-10-16 docstring-staleness audit."  # c22e
